GPU: D3DTEXF_GAUSSIANCUBIC as the console's convolution filter

The XDK's lazy texture stage setup (CS 0x30F2D0..0x30F3B6) turns a min or mag filter of D3DTEXF_GAUSSIANCUBIC (5)
into NV097_SET_TEXTURE_FILTER MIN = CONVOLUTION_2D_LOD0 (7), MAG = CONVOLUTION_2D_LOD0 (4) and CONVOLUTION_KERNEL =
GAUSSIAN_3 (2) (D3DTEXF_QUINCUNX, 4, gets the QUINCUNX kernel). Both renderers drew it as bilinear. Now a 2D stage
with either filter at 5 takes nine bilinear taps of its top level, one console texel apart, weighted 1 2 1 / 2 4 2 /
1 2 1 over 16, as xemu models the kernel (hw/xbox/nv2a/pgraph/glsl/psh.c); NVIDIA documents no weights. PixelKey's
TexInfo gets kTexGauss (the HLSL gauss3, offsets over texsize, the console size) and the reference renderer's Unit
the same kernel. CS uses it for the bloom's first downsample of the back buffer (0xC1FA0).

